READ-OFF:  delta = (log2 #I_N - log2 n_N)/N  is the index-set surplus per step,
and log2(maxfib)/N is the fibre cost per step.  (AMP*) needs the first
positive and the second -> 0.  They are the SAME number here, identically:
   #I_N = sum over y of fibre(y)  <=  n_N * maxfib ,  so  delta <= log2(maxfib)/N .
That inequality is an identity of the counting, not a property of Collatz.
